      "reviewer_notes": "All 3 gates passed. Gate 1: `liquidate_calculate_seize_ctokens` has a non-test caller at market.move:L750 (main liquidation path). Gate 2: no trust_assumptions defined in BUG_BOUNTY_SCOPE; attack goes through public liquidation entry \u2014 not a trusted data source. Gate 3: market.move is in-scope and liquidation logic is an explicit focus area. An attacker can trigger this via the public liquidation entry point by timing their call when the debt asset's Pyth spot price is transiently above its EMA (a routine condition during upward momentum), causing the seize amount computed with get_spot_price at L1045-1046 to be inflated relative to the EMA-based eligibility check at L998/L1115/L1155, resulting in excess collateral seized from the borrower beyond the protocol's stated incentive. Severity remains Critical: the inconsistency is structural and always exploitable given ordinary market conditions; no oracle compromise or flash loan is required.",
